								<div class="title" id="post-title-2822013">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drbleep" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2887044); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2887044&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606207651" alt="DrBleep" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2887044)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drbleep" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2887044); return false;" >DrBleep</a></span> <span class="odate time_1494876333 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 May 2017 19:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2822013">
									

<p>There were a ton of people who looked at this and critted this over and over and over and I appreciate their help so much. Shaggydredlocks, Rimple, Roget, Weryllium, DrMagnus, AbsentmindedNihilist, Sterbai, Shio, MrWong, Ninevolt, Salvagebar and a whole crap ton of other people that I shopped this around to helped me immensely in formulating and putting this idea to paper. This was a complex concept, and I've been told several times that this was probably deserving of an 001 proposal.</p>
<p>In reality, this is my lead in to my actual 001 proposal. The concept of the SCP is based on the deities from Orcadian Folklore, the Mither of the Sea and Teran, where the Mither is the arthropod, and Teran in all his might and wrath is the Gulper Eel.</p>
<p>The image is under the public domain, and originates from <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PSM_V23_D086_The_deep_sea_fish_eurypharynx_pelecanoides.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PSM_V23_D086_The_deep_sea_fish_eurypharynx_pelecanoides.jpg</a>, the original source from which Wikimedia commons obtained the image is <a href="https://archive.org/details/popularsciencemo23newy">https://archive.org/details/popularsciencemo23newy</a></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Show&nbsp;other&nbsp;stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide&nbsp;other&nbsp;stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Ok, so you know how I said above that the Mither is the lobster, and Teran the eel? That's sort of correct, but not really. It's more like, the lobster and the eel are pieces of the entities, they are puppets, avatars, physical representations for something much larger, and much more powerful. The Foundation doesn't know this when they set the ball in motion, but by tipping the scales in ones favor they have destabilized what was a natural equilibrium. The lobster and eel annihilating each other was just a small scale event, a pinprick with just enough force to disturb a slumbering entity.</p>
</div>
</div>
